# Security

Full detail: `docs/security/SECURITY-BASELINE.md`. Critical bullets also in `project-core`.

## Mandatory

- Server-side authorization; re-check session + role on **every** admin API.
- CSRF protection for mutating operations.
- Secure cookies; strict input validation (Zod).
- Sanitize HTML; forbid arbitrary JS in content.
- MIME + extension checks; file size limits.
- Rate limiting; admin action audit log.
- Content Security Policy; HTTPS only in deployed envs.
- Separate test and production; no secrets in the repository.

## Auth model

- No public registration / profiles / personal cabinets.
- Admin/editor via Google Sign-In (Firebase Auth in approved stack).
- Admin allowlist in DB or environment configuration — never hardcoded in client bundles.
- Client checks are UX only; server is authoritative.

## Content safety

- Drafts/hidden/archived must not leak via public APIs, search index, or previews meant for anonymous users.
- Published media served from controlled storage, not arbitrary remote HTML.

## Never

- Security decisions enforced only on the client.
- Service account with blanket Drive access.
- Committing `.env` secrets, key files, or tokens.
